From a2ab5d62156563a5ff900654ee76c400aaf33e99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:36:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS4: accesses fastmem was declined for share a page table
 walk; host-thread services at VeryHigh

03.92's profile of Mario Kart: in the 60 busiest blocks about 190 accesses walked the page table
and 95 used fastmem. The walking ones were PUSH/POP and stack-frame stores, thread-local storage
reads and memset/memcpy stores: fastmem declined about 240 accesses a second all race long,
nearly all because the 4 KiB guest pages under a 16 KiB host page aren't consecutive or 16
KiB-aligned in the DRAM (thread stacks, local storage), and each declined access was recompiled to
walk the page table on its own: nine walks to push nine registers.

fastmem_declined_shared_walk (A32, on by default): after Optimize, the accesses with a
do_not_fastmem marker (block location and IR name; NamingPass names instructions before any later
pass changes the block, so the markers stay valid) go through A32SharedWalkPass (now taking a
predicate): those through one base register value plus constants share one A32HostPointer walk,
every other access keeps fastmem. The emitters keep the blocks with declined accesses
(blocks_without_fastmem, filled by FastmemCallback).

Host harness, the stack's pages left out of the fastmem arena: a call (PUSH r4-r11, lr; VPUSH
d8-d15; the pops) 55.2 ns with per-access walks, 21.1 shared, 18.1 fastmem, 24.5 without fastmem.
Old build vs new, every option on: 1,208 random programs (split stack, fastmem) equal.

RunHostThreadFunc on the PS4: the services on host threads (audio, nvservices, FS, vi, bsdsocket,
ldn) run at VeryHigh. At the default priority a woken one waited behind the emulated cores'
threads (the fourth spins 50 us when idle), the Vulkan thread and audio: 130 us on average until
it took a call in 03.92, against 77 us of handling.
